<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bilhana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bilhana was an 11th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> poet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> who left his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>, travelled through northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and became court poet of the Western Chalukya king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramaditya-vi">Vikramaditya VI</a> at Kalyani. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikramankadevacharita">Vikramankadevacharita</a>, a verse biography of the king, is an important source for the dynasty's history. He is also credited with the love poem Chaurapanchashika, or Fifty Stanzas of a Thief.</p></div>
